export anchor QuietOpsStyle:
    number: 219
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Quiet ops
    idea: A calm operations console in low chroma greys with hairline rules and tabular figures, where the only colour on screen belongs to status, so anything green, amber or red is news.
    base: light
    palette:
        page: #f3f3f2, the page behind panels
        surface: #ffffff, panels, the header and fields
        sunken: #ebebea, table heads and the avatar
        line: #d6d6d3, hairline rules, panel edges and KPI cell dividers
        edge: #8a8c88, field and secondary button borders
        ink: #1d1e20, text and figures
        ink2: #4f5155, secondary text and chart values
        muted: #63666b, labels, meta and timestamps
        graphite: #2f3134, the primary button, this week bars, progress fills and focus
        bar: #8b8d91, last week bars, never text
        green: #1d6a3c, On track with an outlined circle and check
        amber: #8a5200, At risk with an outlined triangle and bang
        red: #b0261c, Behind with an outlined square and down arrow, and every overdue mark
    type:
        Two stacks. Text uses system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue,
        Arial. Figures, timestamps and task counts use ui-monospace, SF
        Mono, Menlo, Consolas. The greeting is 18px 600, KPI figures 26px
        500 mono, panel titles and column heads 11 to 12px caps tracked
        0.06em, row names 13px 600, body 13px and timestamps 11px mono.
    layout:
        One white header bar 48px tall with a hairline below. It holds a
        small outlined square mark and the brand, then the six nav items
        as text tabs with small grey icons, the current tab underlined in
        graphite. At right sit a 240px search field, a graphite New
        project button, a bell with an outlined count and the avatar with
        Mara Okafor after a hairline. Below, a status line reads Hello,
        Mara and the date at left with 4 tasks are overdue in red with a
        clock at the far right, over a hairline. The four KPIs are one
        white strip split into four cells by hairlines, each a caps label
        over a mono figure and a short grey note, the overdue cell red. The
        body is two columns, a wide left and a 360px right. Left holds the
        projects table with columns for project and department, status,
        a thin 4px progress bar with percent, tasks as 18/25 and due date
        with days left, then the chart panel with fourteen thin bars, grey
        last week and graphite this week, split by a dashed line, values
        printed above and day letter and date below, and a legend with
        the week totals and the change. Right holds a status mix panel
        with a thin three part bar and the counts 4, 1 and 1, then an
        activity log with a mono time column beside each entry. Below
        800px the tabs drop to their own scrolling row and KPIs become two
        by two. Below 640px table rows become small grids and the chart
        scrolls sideways.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 4px inside controls, 8 to 12px cell padding, 16px between panels.
    density: High. 40px table rows and many facts on one screen.
    corners: Square panels. 3px on buttons and fields, and only the avatar is round.
    borders: 1px hairlines around panels, between rows and between KPI cells.
    shadows: None. Depth comes only from grey page against white panels.
    icons:
        16px line icons at 1.8px stroke in grey for nav and tools. Status
        icons are 14px outlined shapes in their status colour, a circle
        with a check, a triangle with a bang, a square with a down arrow,
        and a clock ring for overdue.
    focus: A 2px graphite outline offset 2px on every control.
    tone: Terse and factual, such as Activity log, Status mix and 4 tasks are overdue.
